  "decisions": [
    "Low: up to 480p, FXAA, simple shadows, direct lighting and distance fog.",
    "Medium: up to 720p, TAA, balanced bounce lighting, contact shading, screen reflections and volumetric haze. GI-off candidate rejected after Office visual review.",
    "High: up to 1080p, TAA, finer shadows and contact shading; balanced GI, reflections and fog.",
    "Ultra: up to 1440p, TAA, full effects. Native and combined TAA + 4x MSAA remain manual choices.",
    "Lower modes spend more on Clean image quality than their old 360p/480p/720p counterparts; they are not claimed faster than the old lower presets.",
    "All fixture visibility and practical shadow occlusion retained. No adjacent-room light disabling.",
    "World resolution caps remain 480p with CRT and 720p with tape/receiver; a lower user resolution remains lower.",
    "Video signal/output quality remains tiered separately: signal 240/360/480/480 lines; output 720/1080/1440/native. Ultra video output can remain expensive on Retina.",
    "Saved choices are preserved, and older preset combinations become Custom. Custom world tweaks retain the previous named video budget; selecting a named preset resets video quality to Automatic."
